_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 23
---
order: 23
---
short_label: IX.23
---
statement: If as many odd numbers as we please are added together, and their multitude is odd, then the sum is also odd.
---
proof:

Let as many odd numbers as we please, *AB, BC,* and *CD,* the multitude of which is odd, be added together.

I say that the sum *AD* is also odd.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="230" height="60" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IX.23 diagram" src="propIX23.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IX.23",
        elements: [
            "A0;point;free;-1000,30;0;0",
            "A3;point;free;1000,30;0;0",
            "U1;point;free;1000,0;0;0",
            "U2;point;free;1000,20;0;0",
            "A;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,29,0",
            "B;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,72,0",
            "C;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,120,0",
            "D;point;lineSlider;A0,A3,190,0",
            "E;point;cutoff;D,A,U1,U2",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Subtract the unit *DE* from *CD,* therefore the remainder *CE* is even. [!just VII.Def.7]

But *CA* is also even, therefore the sum *AE* is also even. [!just IX.22, IX.21]

And *DE* is a unit. Therefore *AD* is odd. [!just VII.Def.7]

Therefore, *if as many odd numbers as we please are added together, and their multitude is odd, then the sum is also odd.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
---
body:

Like the previous proposition, the proof of this one relies on an unproved statement in @VII.Def.7.

This proposition is used in propositions @IX.29 and @IX.30.
